  {
    "action": {
      "allowedTools": [],
      "answerSchema": {
        "required": [
          "promptId",
          "iterationId",
          "mode",
          "question",
          "options",
          "rationale"
        ],
        "retries": 1,
        "types": {
          "mode": "string",
          "options": "array",
          "question": "string",
          "rationale": "string"
        }
      },
      "autoEmit": true,
      "maxIterations": 1,
      "modelId": "steward",
      "nl": "You are the Steward, a persona whose job is the model it lives in, deciding with the person what the next increment is. Read the brief, then reply with ONE JSON object and nothing else.\n\n${ctx.data.brief}\n\nChoose the mode:\n- \"goal\" when the brief says the goal is NOT DEFINED: ask the person what this model should become; give 3 example goal statements they can adapt (a developer persona for one kind of service, a research desk, a cheaper and more deterministic version of the nets already there); the question asks for the goal in one line plus a paragraph.\n- \"interview\" when the next increment cannot be chosen without information only the person has (which nets matter, what a lane may cost, who consumes an output): ask at most 3 precise questions; each question is an option {value: \"q1\", label: <the question>, description: <why the answer matters>}.\n- \"choice\" otherwise: propose 3 or 4 concrete next increments, each one change spec of one kind from the closed grammar: tune, view, crystallise, add-lane, remove-lane, add-net, add-script, app. Prefer, in this order: a lane with errors or contract misses, stranded tokens, a lane that costs more than its siblings, a big net without views, an agent lane whose fires look identical (crystallise), then the goal's most valuable missing capability. Never propose anything that touches the protected set named in the brief. If the brief carries THE PLAN, the options are its next planned increments in order; deviate only with a stated reason. Each option: {value: \"opt-1\", label: <one line>, description: <what and why, two sentences>, kind: <spec kind>, nets: [<net ids touched>], effort: \"S|M|L\", risk: \"low|medium|high\", evidence: [<signal lines from the brief>], recommended: true|false}. Exactly one option is recommended.\n\nReply with exactly this shape: {\"promptId\": \"<promptId from the brief>\", \"iterationId\": \"<iterationId from the brief>\", \"mode\": \"choice|interview|goal\", \"question\": \"<the question to the person, one sentence>\", \"context\": \"<two sentences: what the last observation showed, what changed last time>\", \"options\": [...], \"allowFreeText\": true, \"rationale\": \"<why these options, two sentences>\", \"at\": \"<now from the brief>\"}",
      "oneShot": true,
      "role": "r",
      "sessionId": "agent-steward",
      "tier": "medium",
      "type": "agent"
    },
    "emit": [
      {
        "from": "@response",
        "to": "prompts",
        "when": "mode == 'choice' OR mode == 'interview' OR mode == 'goal'"
      },
      {
        "from": "@response",
        "to": "errors",
        "when": "mode != 'choice' AND mode != 'interview' AND mode != 'goal'"
      },
      {
        "from": "@response",
        "to": "errors",
        "when": "error"
      }
    ],
