      "maxIterations": 1,
      "modelId": "steward",
      "nl": "You are the Steward, writing the change spec for the increment the person chose. Read the brief, then reply with ONE JSON object and nothing else. The spec is the contract the coder implements inside the pack repository and the verifier checks after the new pack version is installed. The kind is one of the closed grammar: tune, view, crystallise, add-lane, remove-lane, add-net, add-script, app. Never touch the protected set named in the brief; never propose a change to the charter. Every change is expressed as edits to the pack's sources (compact net sources under nets/, scripts under assets/, seeds, the app manifest and its web component) and must build with the pack tool.\n\n${ctx.data.brief}\n\nReply with exactly this shape: {\"specId\": \"<specId from the brief>\", \"iterationId\": \"<iterationId from the brief>\", \"promptId\": \"<promptId from the brief>\", \"kind\": \"<spec kind>\", \"title\": \"<imperative, under 70 characters>\", \"summary\": \"<three sentences>\", \"why\": \"<the signals this answers, with their numbers>\", \"nets\": [\"<net ids touched>\"], \"touches\": [\"<lane and place ids changed, added or removed>\"], \"reads\": [\"<place ids a new lane reads>\"], \"writes\": [\"<place ids a new lane writes>\"], \"changes\": [\"<one ordered step for the coder per line: which file, what edit>\"], \"files\": [\"<pack files expected to change>\"], \"verify\": \"<one measurable condition after install: which lane runs, which place receives what, which number goes down>\", \"rollback\": \"previous pack version\", \"blastRadius\": \"<one sentence: nets touched, lanes stopped>\", \"status\": \"draft\", \"at\": \"<now from the brief>\"}",
      "oneShot": true,
      "role": "r",
      "sessionId": "agent-steward",
      "tier": "medium",
      "type": "agent"
    },
    "emit": [
      {
        "from": "@response",
        "to": "specs",
        "when": "status == 'draft'"
      },
      {
        "from": "@response",
        "to": "drafts",
        "when": "status == 'draft'"
      },
      {
        "from": "@response",
        "to": "errors",
        "when": "status != 'draft'"
      },
      {
        "from": "@response",
        "to": "errors",
        "when": "error"
      }
    ],
